-- title:
--   The missing coordinate-count index identifies the deleted vertex
-- statement:
--   Work in an $n$-dimensional cubical Sperner grid $\{0,\ldots,p\}^n$. A simplex is an injective ordered list of vertices, nondecreasing in every coordinate, whose first and last vertices differ by at most one in each coordinate.
--
--   Delete vertex $j_1$ from an $n$-simplex $J$. Suppose the resulting sequence of coordinate-change counts from its first vertex is the increasing enumeration of $\{0,\ldots,n\}\setminus\{j_2\}$. Then
--
--   $$j_1=0\Rightarrow j_2=n,\qquad j_1\ne0\Rightarrow j_2=j_1.$$
--
--   This records how deleting the first vertex changes the reference point for the counts.
-- source:
--   https://prove2.me/submissions/facf5b05-d302-42c1-a107-8ff40a0c2134; delete_vertex_ccc_fun_match, lines 2460-2542

